  "question": {
    "text": "Electrolysis of hot aqueous solution of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math> gives <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math> , i.e., sodium perchlorate,<br />\r<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>↑</mo></math><br />\rHow many Faraday are required to obtain <math><mn>1000&nbsp;</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of sodium perchlorate? Report your answer by rounding it up to nearest whole number."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "66",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Equivalent mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mtext>Molecular&nbsp;mass</mtext><mtext>Change&nbsp;in&nbsp;oxidation&nbsp;state&nbsp;of&nbsp;chloride</mtext></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>122.5</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>15.13</mn></math><br />Number of Faraday = Number of equivalent of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math> formed<br /><math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1000</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>15.13</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>66</mn></math>"
  }
